From 73bc3ae76da57016b7e427b1c10a2442dc810584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:55:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] rust: fs: add file system registration, superblock and
 inode abstractions

Add a minimal, read-only oriented VFS binding so a file system can be
written in Rust as a loadable module:

- FileSystem trait with fs_context based mounting (get_tree_nodev),
  superblock private data, statfs and inode eviction hooks;
- INode<T> wrapper with per-inode data stored in a container allocated
  through alloc_inode/free_inode, iget_locked based creation (NewINode)
  and lookup/read_iter/iterate_shared/get_link trampolines;
- DirEmitter around dir_emit;
- C helpers for dir_emit, i_size_write, set_delayed_call and
  init_user_ns id mapping.
